## 8. Risk Management
### High-Risk Items
| Area | Risk Level | Description | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|
| Mixed managed/native solution | High | .NET migration can be blocked by unrelated native toolchain gaps | Separate prerequisite gate before atomic managed pass |
| Legacy toolsets (`v90`, `v141_xp`) | High | Missing compilers block validation of native projects/tests | Install required build tools or approve retarget strategy upfront |
| Qt and Windows SDK headers | High | Missing includes (`QtCore/QMap`, `windows.h`) stop compilation | Standardize SDK/Qt configuration before full build validation |
| `ipn_tool` API delta (79 incidents) | High | Highest managed compatibility churn | Prioritize focused code review and regression tests |
| Behavioral API changes | Medium | Runtime drift not always caught by compile step | Extend targeted tests for behavioral hotspots |

### Security Posture
- Assessment did not report explicit vulnerable package list.
- Legacy crypto findings are treated as security-relevant modernization work and should be remediated during upgrade.

### Contingency Plan
- If full-solution validation is blocked by native toolchain constraints, complete managed atomic upgrade validation first, then execute native remediation track with explicit acceptance criteria.
- Maintain rollback point before atomic managed change set.


